Where the hypothesis gives out
==============================================================================
  (C) is not free: it must fail somewhere, since three bodies pushed
  together stop having three peaks at all. Sweeping an isosceles
  triangle from wide to tight at sigma = 0.30:

      base     delta   slack in (C)      lam_max  three peaks?
      2.00    0.0000      9.000e-02   -1.111e+01           yes
      1.50    0.0000      8.998e-02   -1.111e+01           yes
      1.20    0.0007      8.909e-02   -1.103e+01           yes
      1.00    0.0071      8.249e-02   -1.044e+01           yes
      0.90    0.0201      7.122e-02   -9.452e+00           yes
      0.80    0.0560      4.427e-02   -7.173e+00           yes
      0.75    0.0987      1.596e-02   -4.916e+00           yes
      0.70         -              -            -            no
      0.65         -              -            -            no

  So (C) and the existence of the diagram give out together, which is
  the right behaviour: where there is a vineyard to speak of, the
  hypothesis holds.

  verdict inside the note's window and on random triangles: (C) holds and the conclusion holds
